---
// Questions a reader of the leaderboard asks first.
import { asset } from '../../lib/data';
---
<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <details><summary>How do these numbers relate to the paper?</summary><p>The paper reports the 9 core tasks: the “9 core” view of the board, where the learned policies sit beside the agents. The live board adds 11 extended tasks and models released since. The paper’s own page is <a href={asset('/paper/')}>here</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why are some models shown at two efforts?</summary><p>Smaller models gain a lot from a higher reasoning effort, frontier models little. We show every effort we ran and join them, rather than pick one.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does an agent get?</summary><p>One demonstration video, the robot’s head and wrist cameras at 84×84, its joint readings, and 101,000 simulation steps per session. No inverse kinematics, no calibration, no external camera.</p></details>
    <details open><summary>How do I add a model?</summary><p>Email its results on every task, with the final programs and session logs, to <a href="mailto:jz5725@ic.ac.uk">jz5725@ic.ac.uk</a>. We re-score the programs on our evaluation seeds before listing them, and can run a model ourselves if you prefer: all 20 tasks, 3 sessions each, in its maker’s own coding harness.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq { padding-block: 3.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.2rem); }
  details { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: 0.85rem; max-width: 50rem; font-family: var(--sans); }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  details p { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
